# Never commit original game data or anything extracted from it.
# See CLAUDE.md, "Clean-room boundary". The pre-commit hook enforces this too.

*.win
game.ios
*.unx
*.audiogroup
gml_dump/
oracle/

# Extracted assets
*.png
# ...except the curated sprite set the browser build ships. CLAUDE.md accepts
# bundling sprites (free, non-commercial). 96 sprites / 271 frames / ~1.1 MB,
# only what the fight code references.
!assets/sprites/*.png
# The battle UI draws item and ACT names with a REAL font asset (fnt_mainbig),
# not the digit-only sprite fonts. Same posture as the sprites: extracted from
# the player own copy, free and non-commercial.
!assets/fonts/*.png
*.wav
*.ogg
*.mp3

# Generated traces — regenerate with tools/run-trace.mjs, never commit
/traces/
*.csv

node_modules/
/build/
/output/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# AUDIO NOW SHIPS. The earlier stance here was that the soundtrack is sold
# separately so nothing audio could go in the repo; CLAUDE.md now records that
# the sound effects are specifically permitted by Toby Fox and Sebastian Wolf,
# so the SFX travel with the build like the sprites do.
#
# MUSIC SHIPS TOO now — the sound effects AND the soundtrack are recorded in
# CLAUDE.md as permitted. The fight's track is `knight.ogg`, which the game
# loads as a LOOSE FILE (`snd_init("knight.ogg")` out of Resources/mus/)
# rather than packed into an audiogroup like the SFX, so it needed no
# extraction pass at all — only a copy.
!assets/audio/*.wav
!assets/audio/index.json
!assets/audio/*.ogg
